## Verdict: NO-GO

The current controller/launcher cannot admit an ABBA campaign or performance promotion. It has meaningful defensive pieces, but the executable trust chain, terminal durability, raw-evidence derivation, immutable build identity, and final-promotion semantics remain open.

### P0 — Typed promotion is premature and false

After eight diagnostic slots, the launcher performs one recensus, calls the diagnostic cohort comparator, and writes `promoted: true` immediately: [launch.rs:547](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/xtask/src/architecture/assay/launch.rs:547), [launch.rs:558](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/xtask/src/architecture/assay/launch.rs:558), [launch.rs:868](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/xtask/src/architecture/assay/launch.rs:868).

The authority requires a fresh B-only release build, recensus, and two governing twins after diagnostic benefit: [P3.1-ARM-SHA-SUCCESSOR-AUTHORITY.md:96](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/restart/skinny/tranches/sk-v25/graph/P3.1-ARM-SHA-SUCCESSOR-AUTHORITY.md:96). The protocol explicitly says performance credit remains zero until that stage: [P3.1-ARM-SHA-ASSAY-PROTOCOL.md:180](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/restart/skinny/tranches/sk-v25/graph/P3.1-ARM-SHA-ASSAY-PROTOCOL.md:180).

No release-promotion state, request, CLI action, or B-only twin type exists. The outcome must distinguish diagnostic benefit from final promotion.

### P0 — The external driver remains an unverified oracle

The request accepts an arbitrary bound driver binary: [launch.rs:105](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/xtask/src/architecture/assay/launch.rs:105). The controller delegates pre-spawn measurement, launch, and final recensus to it: [launch.rs:299](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/xtask/src/architecture/assay/launch.rs:299). There is no production driver implementation in the inspected source.

Consequently, controller code never proves that the driver actually used:

- `/usr/bin/time -lp`;
- the bound exporter and output path;
- `/usr/bin/sample <exact-pid> 120 1`;
- the claimed exporter environment;
- the claimed sysctl/pmset/ps commands;
- the claimed no-write censuses.

Host and recensus transcripts are opaque bytes whose typed summaries are supplied by the same driver: [launch.rs:578](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/xtask/src/architecture/assay/launch.rs:578), [launch.rs:701](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/xtask/src/architecture/assay/launch.rs:701). The tests demonstrate this trust boundary by synthesizing arbitrary passing host and PID receipts: [assay_launch.rs:149](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/xtask/tests/architecture/assay_launch.rs:149).

A hash-bound binary is not enough without a bound driver source/runtime/tool receipt and controller-derived command/PID facts.

### P0 — Crash/restart durability and no-retry semantics are not closed

The launch request CAS object is created before the first state transition: [launch.rs:421](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/xtask/src/architecture/assay/launch.rs:421). Reopening after a crash and attempting the same request fails because object reuse is forbidden: [state.rs:777](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/xtask/src/architecture/assay/state.rs:777).

Additional unrecoverable windows include:

- subject directory and manifest persisted before the slot state: [state.rs:910](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/xtask/src/architecture/assay/state.rs:910), [state.rs:1161](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/xtask/src/architecture/assay/state.rs:1161);
- crash after pre-spawn or readiness persistence;
- crash after child spawn and before readiness/go;
- crash between outcome CAS storage and external outcome publication: [launch.rs:876](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/xtask/src/architecture/assay/launch.rs:876).

The launcher always restarts iteration at A1 rather than resuming the journaled active slot: [launch.rs:434](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/xtask/src/architecture/assay/launch.rs:434). There is no campaign ownership lock, recovery record, or persisted final disposition.

Preflight failures before the loop—artifact validation, campaign opening, or request CAS failure—also return without terminalizing the campaign or writing an outcome.

### P0 — Campaign authority and the required one-way subject manifest are absent

`authority_hash` is merely self-hashed manifest data and is never checked against the authority file: [state.rs:79](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/xtask/src/architecture/assay/state.rs:79), [state.rs:118](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/xtask/src/architecture/assay/state.rs:118). The closure subject is opaque bytes, and request/campaign linkage checks only slot reservations: [launch.rs:795](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/xtask/src/architecture/assay/launch.rs:795).

RUN-ledger row 292 required a one-way RUN-prefix subject manifest: [RUN-LEDGER.md:292](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/restart/skinny/tranches/sk-v25/RUN-LEDGER.md:292). None exists. The old whole-file cycle remains because the S2 ledger still hashes `RUN-LEDGER.md`: [P3.1-ARM-SHA-S2-LEDGER.tsv:15](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/restart/skinny/tranches/sk-v25/graph/P3.1-ARM-SHA-S2-LEDGER.tsv:15).

