Artifact validation occurs before a driver pre-spawn operation that may last twenty minutes, leaving a large check/use replacement window: [launch.rs:573](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/xtask/src/architecture/assay/launch.rs:573).

Exact semantic tool closure is also incomplete for script-like tools: a non-Mach-O executable is accepted as “static-or-non-mach-o” without binding its shebang interpreter: [binding.rs:2261](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/xtask/src/architecture/evidence/binding.rs:2261).

### P0 — Raw opcode, profile, and vector derivation remains forgeable

- The disassembly is externally supplied text. `OpcodeReceipt::derive` parses mnemonic strings but never proves that the text was produced from the bound exporter, never validates raw instruction words, and never checks `nm`: [receipt.rs:276](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/xtask/src/architecture/assay/receipt.rs:276).
- Production code does not use `NumericOpcodeExpectation`; exact frozen counts are exercised only by tests. Production merely requires each mnemonic count to be nonzero: [receipt.rs:400](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/xtask/src/architecture/assay/receipt.rs:400).
- No-soft-alternative proof exists. B may contain one hardware body plus an unreported software compression body.
- B sample-address TSV is externally supplied and range-checked, but never derived from the raw `sample` transcript or its Binary Images/ASLR mapping: [state.rs:1066](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/xtask/src/architecture/assay/state.rs:1066).
- Vector JSON is validated against constants, but there is no PID/process proof that the lane binary executed the vector action in that slot: [state.rs:994](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/xtask/src/architecture/assay/state.rs:994).

### P0 — PID/readiness gating is incomplete

`S2ExternalChild` does not expose the actual driver child PID: [launch.rs:249](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/xtask/src/architecture/assay/launch.rs:249). Readiness therefore accepts driver-asserted time/exporter/sample PIDs.

The controller hashes but does not parse the process tree: [launch.rs:1003](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/xtask/src/architecture/assay/launch.rs:1003). It proves neither parentage nor sample attachment to the exporter.

The two phases do not implement the protocol’s CPU exclusion law:

- pre-spawn snapshot contains CPU totals but no child tree;
- readiness contains PIDs but no post-spawn outside-tree CPU totals.

Timeout termination kills only the driver process, not a process group or exporter/time/sample descendants: [launch.rs:290](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/xtask/src/architecture/assay/launch.rs:290).

### P1 — Documentation and code disagree on frozen commands and authority

The protocol calls these the exact admissible build commands but omits `-vv` and `--offline`: [P3.1-ARM-SHA-ASSAY-PROTOCOL.md:11](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/restart/skinny/tranches/sk-v25/graph/P3.1-ARM-SHA-ASSAY-PROTOCOL.md:11). Code requires both: [assay.rs:185](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/xtask/src/architecture/assay.rs:185).

The authority says the measured assay is authorized: [P3.1-ARM-SHA-SUCCESSOR-AUTHORITY.md:3](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/restart/skinny/tranches/sk-v25/graph/P3.1-ARM-SHA-SUCCESSOR-AUTHORITY.md:3), while the latest adjudicated ledger row authorizes only P0 repair and expressly forbids a diagnostic build or ABBA: [RUN-LEDGER.md:292](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/restart/skinny/tranches/sk-v25/RUN-LEDGER.md:292).

The protocol demands frozen numeric opcode counts but supplies no numeric authority, while production enforces only positive counts.

### P1 — Symlink, alias, and concurrent mutation defenses are incomplete

Campaign opening validates root member names but does not reject a symlinked `manifest.json`, `states` parent, or `subjects` parent: [state.rs:682](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/xtask/src/architecture/assay/state.rs:682), [state.rs:700](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/xtask/src/architecture/assay/state.rs:700).

Fresh launcher paths are compared textually, without inode/hardlink or filesystem identity checks: [launch.rs:720](/Users/mkbabb/Programming/bbnf-lang/xtask/src/architecture/assay/launch.rs:720). File verification uses metadata/read/path sequences rather than descriptor-owned execution, leaving replacement races.

No exclusive campaign lock prevents two different launch requests from acting on one pending state concurrently.

### P1 — Total-tranche fit and KISS remain RED

The assay surface is approximately 5,962 production lines plus 1,256 focused test lines, yet:

- there is no production driver;
- there is no full successful eight-slot launcher test;
- there is no fresh B-only promotion wave;
- there is no crash recovery;
- the underlying P3.1 tranche and movement remain globally RED.

The measured SHA hotspot justifies a narrow assay, but this wave has created a second transaction/build/CAS/driver framework without closing its essential trust roots. Complexity is concentrated in typed receipts while the actual command execution and evidence derivation remain external and unproved.

